ts limit is $\\dfrac 1 3.$" 13194139533389 17592186045585 true] [17592186096561 1071 "![](images/eb/eb7118486df97c3abae6c8492170090df0c654064799e04826a39a94bcfa22a8.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=\\sqrt{x+1}$, the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=0$ and $y=1$, as shown above." 13194139533389 17592186045585 false] [17592186096561 1071 "![](images/eb/eb7118486df97c3abae6c8492170090df0c654064799e04826a39a94bcfa22a8.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=\\sqrt{x+1},$ the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=0$ and $y=1,$ as shown above." 13194139533389 17592186045585 true] [17592186096561 1074 "First, we make $x$ the subject:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= \\sqrt{x + 1} \\\\\ny^{2} &= x + 1 \\\\\nx &= y^{2} - 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\int_{0}^{1}(y^{2} - 1)dy \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{1}y^{2}dy - \\int_{0}^{1}dy \\\\\n&= \\left.\\frac{y^{3}}{3}\\right|_{0}^{1} - \\left.y\\right|_{0}^{1} \\\\\n&= (\\frac{1}{3} - 0) - (1 - 0) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3} - 1 \\\\\n&=-\\frac{2}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe obtained a negative number because the region lies to the left of the $y$-axis. So the area that we want is\n\n$$\n\\left|-\\dfrac{2}{3}\\right| = \\dfrac{2}{3}\n$$" 13194139533389 17592186045585 false] [17592186096561 1074 "First, we make $x$ the subject:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt{x+1} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =x+1 \\\\ x & ={y}^{2}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{1}-y{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3}-0)-(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}-1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe obtained a negative number because the region lies to the left of the $y$-axis. So the area that we want is $\\left|-\\dfrac{2}{3}\\right| = \\