k\n    \\matrix {\n        2 & -5\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack\n\n\t&= \n\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n        (-1)\\cdot 2 & (-1)\\cdot (-5) \\\n        0\\cdot 2 & 0\\cdot (-5)\\\n        (-2)\\cdot 2 & (-2)\\cdot (-5)\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack \\[5pt]\n\n\t&=\n\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n       -2 & 5 \\\n       0 &  0 \\\n       -4 &  10 \n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack \n}\n$$" 13194139533389 17592186045585 true] [17592186100755 1071 "The values of functions $p(x)$ and $q(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=-3$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $p(x)$ | $q(x)$ | $p'(x)$ | $q'(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-3$ | $1$ | $8$ | $0$ | $-2$ |\n\nCompute $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\big( p(x) + 5q(x) \\big)$ at $x=-3.$" 13194139533389 17592186045585 true] [17592186100755 1071 "The values of functions $p(x)$ and $q(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=-3$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $p(x)$ | $q(x)$ | $p'(x)$ | $q'(x)$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $-3$ | $1$ | $8$ | $0$ | $-2$ |\n\nCompute $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\big(p(x) + 5q(x) \\big)$ at $x=-3$." 13194139533389 17592186045585 false] [17592186100755 1074 "Using the sum and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left( p(x) + 5q(x) \\right) = p'(x) + 5q'(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=-3$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(p(x)+5q(x))|}_{x=-3} & ={p}^{′}(-3)+5{q}^{′}(-3) \\\\  & =0+5\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533389 17592186045585 true] [17592186100755 1074 "Using the sum and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(p(x) + 5q(x) \\right) = p'(x) + 5q'(x)\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=-3$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left.\\frac{d}{dx}(p(x) + 5q(x))\\right|_{x =-3} &= p^{′}(-3) + 5q^{′}(-3) \\\\\n&= 0 + 5 \\cdot (-2) \\\\\n&=-10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533389 17592186045585 false] [17592186100756 1071 "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=0$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | $f'(x)$ | $g'(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $3$ | $-2$ | $0$ |\n\nCompute $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\big(f(x)g(x)\\big)$ at $x=0.$" 13194139533389 17592186045585 true] [17592186100756 1071 "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=0$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | $f'(x)$ | $g'(x)$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $3$ | $-2$ | $0$ |\n\nCompute $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\big(f(x)g(x)\\big)$ at $x=0$." 13194139533389 17592186045585 false] [17592186100756 1074 "Using the product rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\big(f(x)g(x)\\big) = f(x)g'(x)+f'(x)g(x)\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=0$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left.\\frac{d}{dx}(f(x)g(x))\\right|_{x = 0} &= f(0)g^{′}(0) + f^{′}(0)g(0) \\\\\n&= 1 \\cdot 0 + 3 \\cdot (-2) \\\\\n&=-6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533389 17592186045585 false] [17592186100756 1074 "Using the product rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\big(f(x)g(x)\\big) = f(x)g'(x)+f'(x)g(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=0$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=0} & =f(0){g}^{′}(0)+{f}^{′}(0)g(0) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0+3\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533389 17592186045585 true] [17592186100759 1071 "Find the left- and right-sided limits at $x=1$ of the piecewise function $f(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6{e}^{x-1}\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x<1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2x+3\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x>1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533389 17592186045585 true] [17592186100759 1071 "Find the left- and right-sided limits at $x=1$ of the piecewise function $f(x)$ defined by\n${6e^{x - 1}\\begin{vmatrix}forx < 1 \\\\ x^{2} + 2x + 3\\end{vmatrix}forx > 1$." 13194139533389 17592186045585 false] [17592186100759 1074 "Appr