ed}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, let $\\theta = m\\angle{AOB}$ be the angle between the vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}.$ Then, we can find $\\cos \\theta$ using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{‖a‖\\,‖b‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{1}{b}_{1}+{a}_{2}{b}_{2}+{a}_{3}{b}_{3}+{a}_{4}{b}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{1}^{2}+{a}_{2}^{2}+{a}_{3}^{2}+{a}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{b}_{1}^{2}+{b}_{2}^{2}+{b}_{3}^{2}+{b}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)\\cdot 4+4\\cdot 0+(-2)\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot (-4)}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-4)^{2}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{-14}{\\sqrt{28}\\cdot \\sqrt{33}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-14}{\\sqrt{14}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{33}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{33}} \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{33}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533389 17592186045585 true] [17592186133637 1074 "First, let\n\n$$\na = OA^(→) = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}, b = OB^(→) = \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nAlso, let\n\n$$\n\\theta = m\\angle{AOB}\n$$\n\nbe the angle between the vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$. Then, we can find $\\cos \\theta$ using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos θ &= \\frac{a \\cdot b}{‖a‖‖b‖} \\\\\n&= \\frac{a_{1}b_{1} + a_{2}b_{2} + a_{3}b_{3} + a_{4}b_{4}}{\\sqrt{a_{1}^{2} + a_{2}^{2} + a_{3}^{2} + a_{4}^{2}}\\sqrt{b_{1}^{2} + b_{2}^{2} + b_{3}^{2} + b_{4}^{2}}} \\\\\n&= ((-2) \\cdot 4 + 4 \\cdot 0 + (-2) \\cdot (-1) + 2 \\cdot (-4))/(\\sqrt{(-2)^{2} + 4^{2} + (-2)^{2} + 2^{2}}\\sqrt{4^{2} + 0^{2} + (-1)^{2} + (-4)^{2}})) \\\\\n&= \\frac{-14}{\\sqrt{28} \\cdot \\sqrt{33}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{-14}{\\sqrt{14} \\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\cdot \\sqrt{33}} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{\\sqrt{2} \\cdot \\sqrt{33}} \\\\\n&=-\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{33}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533389 17592186045585 false] [17592186133638 1071 "Consider the vector subspace ![](images/be/bee23