** | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** | **$6$** |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $y$ | $40$ | $70$ | $120$ | $100$ | $80$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients of the curve $y = \\beta_0 + \\beta_1 x + \\beta_2 x^2 + \\beta_3 x^3$ that best fits the data above can be found using polynomial regression as\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}β_{0} \\\\ β_{1} \\\\ β_{2} \\\\ β_{3}\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $\\mathbf{y}$ is the observation vector. Find $X$ and $\\mathbf{y}$ in this context." 13194139533389 17592186045585 false] [17592186133641 1074 "| $x$ | **$\\color{blue}2$** | **$\\color{blue}3$** | **$\\color{blue}4$** | **$\\color{blue}5$** | **$\\color{blue}6$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $\\color{red}40$ | $\\color{red}70$ | $\\color{red}120$ | $\\color{red}100$ | $\\color{red}80$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the curve\n\n$$\ny = \\beta_0 + \\beta_1 x + \\beta_2 x^2 + \\beta_3 x^3\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution ${\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\beta}}}$ to the system\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & {2}^{2} & {2}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 3 & {3}^{2} & {3}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 4 & {4}^{2} & {4}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 5 & {5}^{2} & {5}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 6 & {6}^{2} & {6}^{3}\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2} \\\\ {\\beta }_{3}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}40 \\\\ 70 \\\\ 120 \\\\ 100 \\\\ 80\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta$ is the parameter vector, and $\\mathbf{y}$ is the observation vector." 13194139533389 17592186045585 true] [17592186133641 1074 "| $x$ | **$\\color{blue}2$** | **$\\color{blue}3$** | **$\\color{blue}4$** | **$\\color{blue}5$** | **$\\color{blue}6$** |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $y$ | $\\color{red}40$ | $\\color{red}70$ | $\\color{red}120$ | $\\color{red}100$ | $\\color{red}80$ |\n