g $m = n-2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n2\\sum_{m=0}^\\infty (m+2) (m+1) a_{m+2} x^{m} +\\sum_{n=0}^\\infty a_n x^{n} = 0.\n$$\n\nReplacing $m$ with $n$ in the first summation (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\n2\\sum_{n=0}^\\infty (n+2) (n+1) a_{n+2} x^{n} +\\sum_{n=0}^\\infty a_n x^{n} = 0.\n$$\n\nSince both sums now start with $n=0,$ we can combine them as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }2(n+2)(n+1){a}_{n+2}{x}^{n}+{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n} & =0 \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }[2(n+2)(n+1){a}_{n+2}{x}^{n}+{a}_{n}{x}^{n}] & =0 \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }[2(n+2)(n+1){a}_{n+2}+{a}_{n}]{x}^{n} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting each coefficient of $x$ equal to zero, we obtain\n\n$$\n2(n+2)(n+1) a_{n+2}  +a_n = 0.\n$$\n\nFinally then, the recursion formula is\n\n$$\na_{n+2} = -\\dfrac{ a_n }{ 2(n+1)(n+2)  }, \\qquad n= 0,1,2 \\ldots\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nf(n)=-2(n+1)(n+2).\n$$" 13194139533389 17592186045585 true] [17592186147377 1071 "Let ![](images/2a/2ad87a5ee9c27f6d3f03b098b804613d81bc91bb5a811b7655e12efcb052f1e8.png) be a series solution to the equation ![](images/53/5379e686b1ac80c3cb5fec6c41ae2e281b7db590044ff70ff9c3068ac1332f98.png)\n\nWhat is the recurrence relation for the coefficients ![](images/52/527b41b4ced63af6b53983c8aee27c21a7651f52abd01b7600d4e2a1102db63f.png) where ![](images/6c/6ce3483e55b55dee0411597e321facef4f770900e379d1f82da2ceaf278ef40c.png)?" 13194139533389 17592186045585 true] [17592186147377 1071 "Let $y =\\displaystyle{\\sum_{n=0}^\\infty a_n x^n}$ be a series solution to the equation $y' +4xy = 0$.\n\nWhat is the recurrence relation for the coefficients $a_n$, where $n=1,2,3 \\ldots$" 13194139533389 17592186045585 false] [17592186147377 1074 "First, we find ![](images/29/29dbde1998029c25aedffc9dccb1bbaf47781dc5816a69da0256952d82009ef0.png)\n![](images/c7/c7cbd7b8775ba357aa88d794e686d33d0e0474bcea14020d5067fa58175ca159.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the expressions for ![](images/46/4680