\n$$\n\nwhere $m_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}$.\n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{i-1}$ and $y_i$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below.\n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) = x+2y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n- $f(x,y) = x+2y$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/67/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y$. This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/51/51808df96cf7dd295bfa24aa3641a601c821116e1a0014898ffe705036704a53.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm_{ij} &= f(x_{i - 1}, y_{j - 1}) = x_{i - 1} + 2y_{j - 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all\n\n$$\n1\\leq i\\leq m\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n1\\leq j\\leq n\n$$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL(f, P) &= ∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)(x_{i - 1} + 2y_{j - 1})Δx_{i}Δy_{j}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533389 17592186045585 false] [17592186151947 1074 "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $m_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{i-1}$ and $y_i$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) = x+2y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y) = x+2y$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/67/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* 