17592186152014 1074 "First, we find the roots of the characteristic polynomial by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +25 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +9)-9+25 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}-3)^{2}+16 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)^{2} & =-16 \\\\ \\lambda -3 & =4\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =3\\pm 4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following general solution:\n\n$$\ny = e^{3x} \\left( P \\cos 4x + Q \\sin 4x \\right)\n$$\n\nWe find the constants $P$ and $Q$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0) = 2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n2 = P.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition $y'(0) = 5,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =3{e}^{3x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)+{e}^{3x}(-4P\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+4Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $y'(0) = 5$ and $P=2$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =3{e}^{0}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡0+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡0)+{e}^{0}(-4(2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡0+4Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\ 5 & =6+4Q \\\\ -1 & =4Q \\\\ Q & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny = e^{3x} \\left( 2 \\cos 4x - \\dfrac{1}{4} \\sin 4x \\right).\n$$" 13194139533389 17592186045585 true] [17592186152022 1071 "Find $\\textrm{Im}(k)$ given that\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-4\\textrm{i} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$\\begin{bmatrix}8\\textrm{i} - 12 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139533389 17592186045585 false] [17592186152022 1071 "Find $\\textrm{Im}(k)$ given that \n![](images/8c/8c8e19d20f1b580e66eeb558341b4544d2785eb27ab602db7a221a6d9d80eefc.png)\nand\n![](images/2d/2d9551b937b1e8be3c56db51ca26943e1436e07acebc1bfb0f89c16e5e7dcafc.png)" 13194139533389 17592186045585 true] [17592186152022 1074 "Since\n\n$$\n\\overline{k\\mathbf{v}} = \\overline{k} \\, \\overline{\\mathbf{v}}\n$$\n\nwe get the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nkv^(―) &= k^(―)v^(―) \\\\\n\\begin{bmatrix}8\\textrm{i} - 12 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} &= k^(―)\\begin{bmatrix}-4\\textrm{i} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}^(―) \\\\\n\\begin{bmatrix}8\\textrm{i} - 12 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} &= k^(―)\\begin{bmatrix}-4\\textrm{i}^(―) \\\\ 0^(―)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n\\begin{bmatrix}8\\textrm{i} - 12 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} &= k^(―)\\begin{bmatrix}4\\textrm{i} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n\\begin{bmatrix}8\\textrm{i} - 12 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}4\\textrm{i}k^(―) \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain that\n\n$$\n4\\textrm{i}\\,\\overline{k} = 8\\textrm{i}-12 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad \\overline{k}=\\dfrac{8\\textrm{i}-12}{4\\textrm i} = 2+3\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nk=\\overline{2+3\\textrm{i}}=2-3\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Im}(k)=-3\n$$" 13194139533389 17592186045585 false] [17592186152022 1074 "Since $\\overline{k\\mathbf{v}} = \\overline{k} \\, \\overline{\\mathbf{v}},$ we get the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{kv} & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,\\overset{―}{v} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}8\\text{i}-12 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,\\overset{―}{[\\begin{aligned}-4\\text{i} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}8\\text{i}-12 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{-4\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{0}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}8\\text{i}-12 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,[\\begin{aligned}4\\text{i} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}8\\text{i}-12 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4\\text{i}\\,\\overset{―}{k} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain that \n\n$$\n4\\textrm{i}\\,\\overline{k}  = 8\\textrm{i}-12\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\\overline{k}=\\dfrac{8\\textrm{i}-12}{4\\textrm i} = 2+3\\textrm{i}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $k=\\overline{2+3\\textrm{i}}=2-3\\textrm{i}.$\n\nFinally, $\\textrm{Im}(k)=-3.$" 13194139533389 17592186045585 true] [17592186157075 1071 "![](images/1e/1ee7ef0a95e618121f4e0653c6beaa6