 17592186045585 false] [17592186157094 1074 "The set $X \\setminus Y$ is the set of all elements belonging to $X$ but *not* $Y$. Note that the element $5 \\in Y$ is also in $X$, so we must remove it. Hence, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nX∖Y &= X - Y \\\\\n&= {2, 5, 7, 8} - {1, 3, 5} \\\\\n&= {2, 7, 8}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe set $Y \\setminus Z$ is the set of all elements belonging to $Y$ but *not* $Z$. Note that none of the elements of $Y$ are in $Z$. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nY∖Z &= Y - Z \\\\\n&= {1, 3, 5} - {2, 4, 6, 8} \\\\\n&= {1, 3, 5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe set $Z \\setminus X$ is the set of all elements belonging to $Z$ but *not* $X$. Note that the elements $2,8 \\in Z$ are also in $X$, so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nZ∖X &= Z - X \\\\\n&= {2, 4, 6, 8} - {2, 5, 7, 8} \\\\\n&= {4, 6}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533389 17592186045585 false] [17592186157094 1074 "The set $X \\setminus Y$ is the set of all elements belonging to $X$ but *not* $Y.$ Note that the element $5 \\in Y$ is also in $X,$ so we must remove it. Hence, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X∖Y & =X-Y \\\\  & ={2,5,7,8}-{1,3,5} \\\\  & ={2,7,8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe set $Y \\setminus Z$ is the set of all elements belonging to $Y$ but *not* $Z.$ Note that none of the elements of $Y$ are in $Z.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y∖Z & =Y-Z \\\\  & ={1,3,5}-{2,4,6,8} \\\\  & ={1,3,5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe set $Z \\setminus X$ is the set of all elements belonging to $Z$ but *not* $X.$ Note that the elements $2,8 \\in Z$ are also in $X,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Z∖X & =Z-X \\\\  & ={2,4,6,8}-{2,5,7,8} \\\\  & ={4,6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533389 17592186045585 true] [17592186157095 1071 "Let $A$ be the set of all multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ and let $B$ be the set of all multiples of $6$ that are greater than $0$. What is $A \\setminus B$?" 13194139533389 17592186045585 false] [